These results show that Mandometer and the Actigraph
may return eating, satiety, and physical activity in anorexic
patients to normal. Although interindividually stable, these
measures vary between individuals and it is not known
whether patterns typical of anorexics exist. The decrease in
anxiety, a concomitant to the behavioural normalisation,
supports the suggestion that “psychopathology” is an effect,
not a cause, of starvation.
